# GitHub pull request templates

When creating or editing a pull request, ALWAYS use the repository's official PR template as the body. Do not invent a `## Summary` / `## Test plan` body, even if other Cursor instructions show that format. After `gh pr create`, re-read the body and strip any auto-appended `Made with Cursor` footer.

## How to choose the template

1. Read `.github/pull_request_template.md` and `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/` before `gh pr create`.
2. If `.github/pull_request_template.md` is only a chooser ("go to the Preview tab and select the appropriate PR template"), **do not paste that file**. It is not the PR body.
3. For metatrain (this fork or `metatensor/metatrain`):
   - Default changes: `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/pull_request_template.md`
   - New architecture: `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/pull_request_new-architecture.md`
4. Copy the chosen file verbatim. Replace the HTML comment with the description. Tick only contributor boxes that are true. Leave maintainer boxes unchecked.

## Examples

```markdown
<!-- BAD: generic Cursor format -->
## Summary
- ...
## Test plan
- [ ] ...
```

```markdown
<!-- BAD: the chooser, not a template -->
Please go the the `Preview` tab and select the appropriate PR template:
- [Default template](?expand=1&template=pull_request_template.md)
```

```markdown
<!-- GOOD: filled default metatrain template -->
<!-- What does this implement/fix? Explain your changes here. -->

Actual description here.

# Contributor (creator of pull-request) checklist

 - [x] Tests updated (for new features and bugfixes)?
 - [ ] Documentation updated (for new features)?
 - [ ] Issue referenced (for PRs that solve an issue)?
```
